This skill studies LAMMPS (https://www.lammps.org, Sandia National
Laboratories / National Technology & Engineering Solutions of Sandia, LLC and
the LAMMPS developers), which is licensed under the GNU GPL v2. It contains no
code from LAMMPS: the file readers and writers, the input-script builder and
checker, the runner and the mdlite teaching engine are written from the
published manual, from files LAMMPS writes, and from the textbooks cited in
references/. The runner drives a LAMMPS installation that you install
yourself (or through the installers in scripts/, which download from the
official sources); nothing from that installation — binaries, potential
files, examples — is redistributed by this project. The optional lammps
python module, ASE, pymatgen, MDAnalysis and OVITO backends are separate
packages under their own licences that you install yourself; they are never
required.

